  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, which builds the whole handcart from primitives and passes typecheck. I couldn't render it (no shell or browser), so how it looks is unchecked, including prop placement, wheel clearance and shadow softness.\n\n- **Bed:** 16 planks (8 floor, 2 per side wall, 2 per end wall), each with random length, tone and tilt. It has 4 corner posts, 2 cross rails on every side, mid stakes, and iron straps with bolts.\n- **Wheels and axle:** two wheels share one iron axle. Each has a hub with 2 iron bands and a nut, 10 spokes, 14 rim segments and an iron tyre with nails.\n- **Handles and leg:** the frame runners continue rearward as two long sloping push handles with grips. A front prop stand has two legs, feet and a crossbar.\n- **Load:** 3 sacks, 2 barrels with iron hoops, a sack lying across the barrels, and 3 crates (2 on the floor, 1 stacked).\n- **Ground:** a large dirt plane with brown patches and about 17 scattered stones.\n- **Camera and animation:** an orbit camera at three-quarter view turntables slowly. Both wheels also spin in place.\n- **Lighting:** a warm directional sun with shadows, a hemisphere light, a neutral environment, and fog.\n- **Flags:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()`. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is `{ ready: true, wheelCount: 2, spokeCount: 20, plankCount: 16 }`.\n\nI made two assumptions from the type definitions only. The shadow options object (`filter`, `softness`, `fit`) matches the declared types. Single-axis rotations are used throughout, so Euler order shouldn't matter.\n\n",
